 "content": "# Continual-ARC pattern note\n\nTask pattern observed (demo + confirmed correct test): Preserve grid dimensions and all cells except insert color 2 into every blank/background cell (color 1) that lies horizontally between two adjacent-in-order marked cells of the special color. In the demo, special marker was 9 and 2 was inserted between horizontally neighboring 9s; in the solved test, markers were 4 and the same inserted color 2. Thus for each row scan left-to-right: whenever two marked-color cells are separated by exactly one 1, recolor that intervening cell to 2. Do not alter markers/background elsewhere or connect marks across rows. Test submission applying this rule was confirmed correct.\n"
